exports[`checkpoint prioritizes unavailable discovery over polishing an unsupported report 2`] = `
{
  "design": "Before collecting, save research_design with one entry per exact subquestion: subquestion, decision_relevance, alternatives (plausible explanations or comparison options), evidence_needed (observations that distinguish them), stop_condition (what permits a bounded answer). Select the next acquisition by its effect on the answer, not by channel quotas or source counts. After evidence selection save coverage.assessment with answer, reasoning, alternatives_considered, remaining_gaps and next_action. A bounded answer may retain uncertainty; unresolved means the question cannot yet be answered. Use checkpoint to inspect saved assessments, blockers and the next operation. Missing evidence calls for new collection or a narrower explicitly agreed scope, not extra paragraphs.",
  "support": "Claim support_basis defaults to corroborated and requires the project independent-source threshold. Use attributed only for a source_claim faithfully reporting what an identified original says, never for asserting its real-world truth. Use internal_check only for an observation checking arithmetic or consistency within exact originals; show the calculation or contradiction. Both still require semantic review. Causal, comparative, effectiveness and economic generalizations remain corroborated. A source count never establishes causality.",
  "revision": "Treat review revisions as research tasks: missing facts require evidence collection; invalid comparisons require a common basis; unsupported explanations require alternatives and discriminating observations. After repairs, rewrite the affected argument and executive synthesis as a whole. Remove superseded caveats and repetitive qualifications. Do not satisfy review by appending disconnected paragraphs. Keep a clear best-supported answer, its implications and the decisive uncertainty."
}
`;
